  "limitations": [
    "vkQueueSubmit/vkWaitForFences faults are returned from test linker interposition, not by the physical Vulkan driver.",
    "The two GPU buffer copies before each fault and the new-device copy after each fault use real Vulkan 1.0 operations on physical Android GPUs.",
    "At the WAIT fault site the queued command really reaches the driver, but the injected fence-wait error skips waiting; vkDeviceWaitIdle on the healthy real device completes pending work during teardown.",
    "The strict policy and native API-boundary rejection are tested only in the dedicated diagnostic, not production HASHCAT backend_ctx or cryptographic kernel execution.",
    "The executable links Vulkan 1.0 entry points and requests Vulkan 1.0 or 1.1, but the tested physical GPU drivers are newer and the operating systems are not Android 7.0/API24.",
    "Real driver VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST, GPU reset, multithreaded Vulkan contention, and driver-level validation-layer leak instrumentation are not tested."
  ]
